# Redakt environment overrides — copy to .env and uncomment values you
# want to override per-instance (secrets, env-specific connection
# strings, file paths). All vars use the REDAKT_ prefix.
#
# Tunable POLICY (thresholds, allow lists, language settings, limits)
# lives in config.yaml at the repo root and is committed to git.
# Defaults are defined in src/redakt/config.py.
#
# Precedence (highest wins):
#   1. Per-request body params on /api/detect, /api/anonymize
#   2. This file (.env) and shell env vars
#   3. config.yaml
#   4. Hard-coded defaults in src/redakt/config.py
#
# Any setting in config.yaml CAN also be overridden here via the
# matching REDAKT_* env var, but the convention is: secrets/paths
# here, policy in config.yaml. Complex types (dicts, lists) are
# JSON-encoded when set via env vars.

# --- Presidio service URLs (env-specific connection strings) ---
# REDAKT_PRESIDIO_ANALYZER_URL=http://localhost:5001
# REDAKT_PRESIDIO_ANONYMIZER_URL=http://localhost:5001

# --- Audit log file path (env-specific filesystem) ---
# REDAKT_AUDIT_LOG_FILE=/var/log/redakt/audit.log

# --- Logging verbosity (env-specific) ---
# REDAKT_LOG_LEVEL=WARNING

# --- Override config.yaml location (rare) ---
# REDAKT_CONFIG_FILE=/etc/redakt/config.yaml
